I think you just change the env you want in your settings example (I don't think there's an easy toggle to the desired kernel):
```
{
  "jupyter": {
    "kernel_selections": {
      "python": "hf_training",
      "typescript": "deno",
      "javascript": "deno",
      "r": "ark"
    }
  }
}

```

@rosszhang1 Indeed, in latest release including your recommendation in `settings.json` and following https://zed.dev/docs/repl#changing-kernels I am able to specify the `kernel` of my liking, i.e.:
```
  "jupyter": {
    "kernel_selections": {
      "python": "core"
    }
```
